WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.930
Rome, AD 336.

2
00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:08.730
Here is the first record of Christians
celebrating Jesus' birth on 25 December.

3
00:00:08.780 --> 00:00:10.080
Why that date?

4
00:00:10.130 --> 00:00:14.540
Historians give two theories: a
Roman winter festival of the Sun,

5
00:00:14.590 --> 00:00:17.960
or a date worked out from 25 March.

6
00:00:18.010 --> 00:00:21.290
In 1647, the Puritan
Parliament went further,

7
00:00:21.340 --> 00:00:23.720
and banned Christmas in England.

8
00:00:23.770 --> 00:00:29.410
So if nobody knows Jesus' real birthday,
why is 25 December one of the biggest

9
00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:31.310
days of the Christian year?

10
00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:34.860
In this mission, you'll compare
two Gospel birth stories:

11
00:00:34.910 --> 00:00:38.810
shepherds in one, wise men
and a star in the other.

12
00:00:38.860 --> 00:00:42.840
Then you'll weigh up whether Christmas in
Britain has lost its religious meaning,

13
00:00:42.890 --> 00:00:45.170
among the shops and the adverts.

14
00:00:45.220 --> 00:00:50.290
Your mission: explain why 25 December
matters so much to Christians.
